---
kind: request
id: 01a041f7-f2ee-75a8-b006-e34dcff214ef
name: GetWeather
assertions:
- status: 200
- header: content-type
  startsWith: text/xml
- xpath: //*[local-name()='Place']
  equals: Amsterdam
- xpath: count(//*[local-name()='Day'])
  equals: '3'
- xpath: //*[local-name()='AuthenticatedAs']
  equals: demo
tags: [demo, soap]
---

```http
POST /demo/soap/weather.asmx
Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8
SOAPAction: "http://demo.tap.dev/weather/GetWeather"

<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
  <soap:Header>
    <wsse:Security soap:mustUnderstand="1" xmlns:wsse="http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-wssecurity-secext-1.0.xsd">
      <wsse:UsernameToken>
        <wsse:Username>{{wsseUsername}}</wsse:Username>
        <wsse:Password Type="http://docs.oasis-open.org/wss/2004/01/oasis-200401-wss-username-token-profile-1.0#PasswordText">{{wssePassword}}</wsse:Password>
      </wsse:UsernameToken>
    </wsse:Security>
  </soap:Header>
  <soap:Body>
    <GetWeather xmlns="http://demo.tap.dev/weather">
      <!-- or: StationId -->
      <CityName>Amsterdam</CityName>
      <Days>3</Days>
      <Units>Celsius</Units>
    </GetWeather>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>
```

# GetWeather

Forecast for a city or a station, up to seven days out.

`Weather/WeatherSoap` · SOAP 1.1 · document/literal · action `http://demo.tap.dev/weather/GetWeather`.

The body is what the WSDL import generated, with real values typed over the placeholders.
The `<!-- or: -->` comment is the importer marking an `xsd:choice`: send `StationId` instead of
`CityName` and the service answers the same shape.

The assertions go through `local-name()` because a SOAP response is namespaced and XPath 1.0 has
no notion of a default namespace — `/Envelope/Body` would match nothing at all.

`AuthenticatedAs` echoes the `<wsse:UsernameToken>` in the header, which is where the collection's
`wsseUsername` / `wssePassword` variables land. Empty the username and the service answers
`xsi:nil` instead.
